{"data": [{"author_id": "59603406", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:33:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120253541507817489"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/federalreserve…", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/federalreserve/status/2120253027131232741", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/JkdsCrDGQk"}]}, "id": "2120253541507817489", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 15306, "like_count": 57, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 12}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120253027131232741", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "On the same day Waller and Logan opened the door to faster hikes, Fed Vice Chair Miki Bowman struck a cautious note: the benefit of more tightening “has to be carefully weighed against its costs” given recent market developments.\n\nIn her remarks, she flags the interconnected https://t.co/JkdsCrDGQk", "url": "https://x.com/NickTimiraos/status/2120253541507817489"}, {"author_id": "26538229", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:31:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120253027131232741"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 111, "id": "17469492", "start": 103, "username": "CFR_org"}], "urls": [{"description": "Good afternoon. It is a pleasure to join you today at the Council on Foreign Relations to discuss my outlook for the U.S. economy. 1 Economic growth has", "display_url": "federalreserve.gov/newsevents/spe…", "end": 136, "expanded_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/speech/bowman20261110a.htm", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120253028754419712/SYnndkYS?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 800}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120253028754419712/SYnndkYS?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 113, "status": 200, "title": "Speech by Vice Chair for Supervision Bowman on the U.S. economy and considerations for monetary policy", "unwound_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/speech/bowman20261110a.htm", "