54742318"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "All services subject to dragons. A small game about public transport and the end of epic quests.", "display_url": "dread-and-district.netlify.app", "end": 283, "expanded_url": "https://dread-and-district.netlify.app", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120248530115997696/n1Fd2YVw?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120248530115997696/n1Fd2YVw?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 260, "status": 200, "title": "Dread & District", "unwound_url": "https://dread-and-district.netlify.app", "url": "https://t.co/1pdsN8Lnov"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/jKOhDWVU2X", "end": 307, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2120248525254742318/video/1", "media_key": "13_2120248122982985728", "start": 284, "url": "https://t.co/jKOhDWVU2X"}]}, "id": "2120248525254742318", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 20, "impression_count": 7943, "like_count": 77, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 39, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Another weird AI game project: I gave Claude Fable 5.2 a vague paragraph asking for a fantasy transport sim with heart. Then I left it to a bunch of agents arguing about art, lore and jokes. Now here is Dread &amp; District, where good logistics defeats evil. https://t.co/1pdsN8Lnov https://t.co/jKOhDWVU2X", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2120248525254742318"}, {"author_id": "15072071", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:15:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120233850064261374"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/FXcc5YVmUJ", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NewYorkFed/status/2120233850064261374/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120233840086077442", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/FXcc5YVmUJ"}]}, "id": "2120233850064261374", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1185, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Register for our third annual FX Market Structure Conference. This event will cover a range of topics related to the foreign exchange market, including the current macro environment and its impact on FX trading activity, trends in FX liquidity and price discovery, the future of https://t.co/FXcc5YVmUJ", "url": "https://x.com/NewYorkFed/status/2120233850064261374"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:14:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120233659793854926"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/GBSHG6EQsS", "end": 192, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2120233659793854926/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120233541887770624", "start": 169, "url": "https://t.co/GBSHG6EQsS"}]}, "id": "2120233659793854926", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 45, "impression_count": 20617, "like_count": 343, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 61, "retweet_count": 17}, "text": "One of the most significant things about Gemini 4 Carbon is that it is showing that Google is back in the race of frontier models, rapid releases and rapid improvement. https://t.co/GBSHG6EQsS", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2120233659793854926"}, {"author_id": "1161370756208648193", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:45:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120226268452905003"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 273, "start": 263, "tag": "IFDPPaper"}], "urls": [{"description": "The Federal Reserve Board of Governors in Washington DC.", "display_url": "federalreserve.gov/econres/ifdp/w…", "end": 262, "expanded_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/ifdp/who-built-the-service-economy.htm", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120226269694459904/ZUOX7EA9?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 800}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120226269694459904/ZUOX7EA9?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 239, "status": 200, "title": "Who Built the Service Economy?", "unwound_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/ifdp/who-built-the-service-economy.htm", "url": "https://t.co/Ufu6iNfs8A"}]}, "id": "2120226268452905003", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 655, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Large incumbent service firms built the US service economy by opening new establishments. In a two-sector firm-dynamics model, cheaper replication costs + rising manufacturing productivity explain over 50% of US structural transformation. https://t.co/Ufu6iNfs8A #IFDPPaper", "url": "https://x.com/FedResearch/status/2120226268452905003"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:56:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120198832202125322"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/IDOdrQtReH", "end": 316, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2120198832202125322/video/1", "media_key": "13_2120198294630526976", "start": 293, "url": "https://t.co/IDOdrQtReH"}]}, "id": "2120198832202125322", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 91, "impression_count": 31328, "like_count": 580, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 93, "retweet_count": 27}, "text": "Had early access to Gemini 4 Carbon, it is a very good model that improves on Argon. It is useful to have an AI that thinks differently than Claude/GPT &amp; is still highly capable, but has its own strengths &amp; weakness\n\nOne fun demo: I gave Carbon a video clip &amp; it reproduced in 3js https://t.co/IDOdrQtReH", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2120198832202125322"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:47:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120196573946949975"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/zVdokob8vB", "end": 99, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2120196573946949975/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120196567755849728", "start": 76, "url": "https://t.co/zVdokob8vB"}]}, "id": "2120196573946949975", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 17922, "like_count": 113, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 21}, "text": "The US-led surge in global bond yields. \n(Bloomberg data.)\n#economy#markets https://t.co/zVdokob8vB", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2120196573946949975"}, {"author_id": "83466368", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:46:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120196475028381704"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "The European Central Bank (ECB) is the central bank of the European Union countries which have adopted the euro. Our main task is to maintain price stability in the euro area and so preserve the purchasing power of the single currency.", "display_url": "link.europa.eu/BBdvwm", "end": 278, "expanded_url": "https://link.europa.eu/BBdvwm", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120196351640346630/mxPqd7AZ?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120196351640346630/mxPqd7AZ?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 255, "status": 200, "title": "The science and practice of monetary policy communication: the ECB experience", "unwound_url": "https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/key/date/2026/html/ecb.sp261110_1~9725b7aa07.en.html", "url": "https://t.co/2dm2ATAmYW"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/69ae6m8xZI", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2120196475028381704/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120195876178006016", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/69ae6m8xZI"}]}, "id": "2120196475028381704", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 4707, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Framework guidance is more effective than rate forward guidance when policy rates are away from the effective lower bound, says Chief Economist Philip R. Lane.\n\nHe also discusses some recent ECB research on monetary policy communication.\n\nRead his speech https://t.co/2dm2ATAmYW https://t.co/69ae6m8xZI", "url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2120196475028381704"}, {"author_id": "15072071", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:39:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120194770135830952"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "NEW YORK — The Federal Reserve Bank of New York’s Center for Microeconomic Data today issued its Quarterly Report on Household Debt and Credit. The report shows total household debt expanded by $334 billion, a 1.8% increase, in Q3 2026, to $19.1 trillion. The report is based on data from the New York Fed’s nationally representative Consumer Credit Panel. It includes a one-page summary of key takeaways and their supporting data points. The New York Fed also issued an accompanying Liberty Street Economics", "display_url": "nyfed.org/4eXmJcg", "end": 229, "expanded_url": "https://nyfed.org/4eXmJcg", "start": 206, "status": 200, "title": "Household Debt Increased Moderately; Delinquency Transition Rates Remain Flat - FEDERAL RESERVE BANK of NEW YORK", "unwound_url": "https://www.newyorkfed.org/newsevents/news/research/2026/20261110", "url": "https://t.co/HPC1E9kEGK"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/UKMCdDrslx", "end": 253, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NewYorkFed/status/2120194770135830952/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120194760811982848", "start": 230, "url": "https://t.co/UKMCdDrslx"}]}, "id": "2120194770135830952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1849, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Today, our Center for Microeconomic Data issued its Quarterly Report on Household Debt and Credit. The report shows total household debt increased by $334 billion in Q3 2026, to $19.1 trillion. Learn more: https://t.co/HPC1E9kEGK https://t.co/UKMCdDrslx", "url": "https://x.com/NewYorkFed/status/2120194770135830952"}, {"author_id": "1161370756208648193", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:35:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120193571357675682"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 14, "start": 4, "tag": "IFDPPaper"}], "urls": [{"description": "The Federal Reserve Board of Governors in Washington DC.", "display_url": "federalreserve.gov/econres/ifdp/t…", "end": 143, "expanded_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/ifdp/trade-deflection-the-spillover-effects-of-us-tariffs-on-import-prices-in-bystander-countries.htm", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120193572557160448/1C2v0uBh?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 800}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120193572557160448/1C2v0uBh?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 120, "status": 200, "title": "Trade Deflection: The Spillover Effects of U.S. Tariffs on Import Prices in Bystander Countries", "unwound_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/ifdp/trade-deflection-the-spillover-effects-of-us-tariffs-on-import-prices-in-bystander-countries.htm", "url": "https://t.co/Z8Qqtwit1d"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Vn05KRFh9h", "end": 167, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/FedResearch/status/2120193571357675682/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120192183030415361", "start": 144, "url": "https://t.co/Vn05KRFh9h"}]}, "id": "2120193571357675682", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 1179, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "New #IFDPPaper: Chinese products targeted by U.S. tariffs see declines in import prices in “bystander” countries. (1/2) https://t.co/Z8Qqtwit1d https://t.co/Vn05KRFh9h", "url": "https://x.com/FedResearch/status/2120193571357675682"}, {"author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:31:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120192683960385939"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 58, "start": 50, "tag": "BLSData"}], "urls": [{"description": "The .gov means it's official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you're on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely. As we observe Veterans Day, let's examine the spending of veteran and active duty military households. In 2025, average annual expenditures for all households were $81,905.", "display_url": "bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/…", "end": 82, "expanded_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/veteran-and-active-duty-military-spending-in-2025.htm", "images": [{"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120192685982052352/3_Bs7t6c?format=png&name=orig", "width": 228}, {"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120192685982052352/3_Bs7t6c?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 126}], "start": 59, "status": 200, "title": "Veteran and active duty military spending in 2025 : The Economics Daily : U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics", "unwound_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/veteran-and-active-duty-military-spending-in-2025.htm", "url": "https://t.co/9en8uY8GXP"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/I3L2up0UON", "end": 106, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2120192683960385939/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120192378417848321", "start": 83, "url": "https://t.co/I3L2up0UON"}]}, "id": "2120192683960385939", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1953, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Veteran and active duty military spending in 2025 #BLSData https://t.co/9en8uY8GXP https://t.co/I3L2up0UON", "url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2120192683960385939"}, {"author_id": "1007413134", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:07:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120186651741655428"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/RYVfMS2vw9", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/DrJimFan/status/2120186651741655428/video/1", "media_key": "13_2120178947035889664", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/RYVfMS2vw9"}]}, "id": "2120186651741655428", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 183, "impression_count": 30956, "like_count": 666, "quote_count": 42, "reply_count": 67, "retweet_count": 94}, "text": "Introducing GR00T 2: our most advanced, open System One model for robotics. It runs entirely on your robot’s onboard compute, fully untethered, and you own every weight of it. GR00T 2 features: \n\n1. Long-horizon tasks: dexterous manipulation and whole-body control chained over https://t.co/RYVfMS2vw9", "url": "https://x.com/DrJimFan/status/2120186651741655428"}, {"author_id": "321536046", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:07:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120186479649464762"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "bea.gov/form/feedback", "end": 150, "expanded_url": "https://bea.gov/form/feedback", "start": 127, "status": 200, "title": "API and Interactive Tables User Survey | U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis (BEA)", "unwound_url": "https://bea.gov/form/feedback", "url": "https://t.co/XHqa96IWZl"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/HLPNAGFMBn", "end": 174, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2120186479649464762/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120186468412837888", "start": 151, "url": "https://t.co/HLPNAGFMBn"}]}, "id": "2120186479649464762", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 724, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Use our API or interactive data tables? We would love your feedback! Find out how to help us improve our data dissemination at https://t.co/XHqa96IWZl https://t.co/HLPNAGFMBn", "url": "https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2120186479649464762"}, {"author_id": "59603406", "created_at": "2026-11-10T15:52:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120182733703967138"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/DallasFed/stat…", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/DallasFed/status/2120160111138119847", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/uEuXI2ea7M"}]}, "id": "2120182733703967138", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 25, "impression_count": 45088, "like_count": 157, "quote_count": 9, "reply_count": 34, "retweet_count": 40}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120160111138119847", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Dallas Fed President Lorie Logan opens the door to a faster pace of rate increases.\n\nHer Oct. 30 speech explained why she was OK with last month's hold. Today, she adds this sentence after the disappointing CPI: \n\n“It may be possible to move more rapidly this winter than the FOMC https://t.co/uEuXI2ea7M", "url": "https://x.com/NickTimiraos/status/2120182733703967138"}, {"author_id": "59603406", "created_at": "2026-11-10T14:53:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120167931992490439"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Gwzryh9R5Y", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NickTimiraos/status/2120167931992490439/video/1", "media_key": "13_2120167762773319680", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/Gwzryh9R5Y"}]}, "id": "2120167931992490439", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 17, "impression_count": 43023, "like_count": 178, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 23, "retweet_count": 27}, "text": "After the firm September PCE inflation reading was released last month, Kevin Hassett allowed that October could return to the lower monthly readings seen in the summer, proving September was \"a blip.\"\n\nBut he added, \"if October comes out really high, then I think the Fed would https://t.co/Gwzryh9R5Y", "url": "https://x.com/NickTimiraos/status/2120167931992490439"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-11-10T14:44:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120165616384651656"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Geopolitical shocks, global fragmentation, and technological change are reshaping growth, inflation, and economic prospects across the Middle East and Central Asia. Policy priorities should include strengthening resilience in a more uncertain world.", "display_url": "imf.org/en/publication…", "end": 237, "expanded_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/reo/meca/issues/2026/10/22/regional-economic-outlook-middle-east-central-asia-october-2026?cid=sm-com-x-am26-REOMCDEA2026002", "images": [{"height": 1080, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119440186354651136/n2ucaWYd?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119440186354651136/n2ucaWYd?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 214, "status": 200, "title": "Regional Economic Outlook for the Middle East and Central Asia, October 2026", "unwound_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/reo/meca/issues/2026/10/22/regional-economic-outlook-middle-east-central-asia-october-2026?cid=sm-com-x-am26-REOMCDEA2026002", "url": "https://t.co/5Jkk0COhsO"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/mcu26CKcar", "end": 261, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2120165616384651656/video/1", "media_key": "13_2120165590509989889", "start": 238, "url": "https://t.co/mcu26CKcar"}]}, "id": "2120165616384651656", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 11315, "like_count": 22, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "MENAP growth is projected to contract by about 1.3% in 2026. Assuming the conflict eases and trade gradually normalizes, growth could rebound to 6.6% in 2027. The economic impact of the war has been highly uneven. https://t.co/5Jkk0COhsO https://t.co/mcu26CKcar", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2120165616384651656"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-11-10T14:29:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120162004275261568"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "External tailwinds are supporting growth across the region despite trade uncertainty and energy price pressures. Policymakers should use this window to reduce debt, preserve pric stability, and raise productivity.", "display_url": "imf.org/en/publication…", "end": 247, "expanded_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/reo/wh/issues/2026/10/16/regional-economic-outlook-for-the-western-hemisphere-october-2026#:~:text=Chapter%202%3A%20The%20Missing%20Link%3A%20From%20Foreign%20Direct%20Investment%20to%20Trade%20and%20Productivity%20Gains%C2%A0%C2%A0", "images": [{"height": 405, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119931064215048192/ppcoSWVn?format=png&name=orig", "width": 400}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119931064215048192/ppcoSWVn?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 224, "status": 200, "title": "Regional Economic Outlook for the Western Hemisphere, October 2026", "unwound_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/reo/wh/issues/2026/10/16/regional-economic-outlook-for-the-western-hemisphere-october-2026#:~:text=Chapter%202%3A%20The%20Missing%20Link%3A%20From%20Foreign%20Direct%20Investment%20to%20Trade%20and%20Productivity%20Gains%C2%A0%C2%A0", "url": "https://t.co/UbuFsVxvtF"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/UXTG60ZMf8", "end": 271, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2120162004275261568/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120162001372737536", "start": 248, "url": "https://t.co/UXTG60ZMf8"}]}, "id": "2120162004275261568", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 15, "impression_count": 12178, "like_count": 62, "quote_count": 6, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 19}, "text": "Latin America and the Caribbean's FDI stock equals 44% of GDP, vs. 25% in emerging Asia and 21% in emerging Europe.\nYet trade integration remains weaker. Why hasn't more FDI meant more exports? Our new REO chapter explains: https://t.co/UbuFsVxvtF https://t.co/UXTG60ZMf8", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2120162004275261568"}, {"author_id": "1161370756208648193", "created_at": "2026-11-10T14:25:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120161036481478897"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 14, "start": 4, "tag": "FEDSPaper"}], "urls": [{"description": "The Federal Reserve Board of Governors in Washington DC.", "display_url": "federalreserve.gov/econres/feds/c…", "end": 122, "expanded_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/feds/costly-misdemeanours-labour-market-effects-of-low-level-drink-driving-violations.htm", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.c